  "thread": {
    "$comment": "EXP-1175: the Run face's THREAD — sessionThread(raw) reads coding_sessions.results in ARRAY (publish) order, the same tolerance and 60-picture cap as parseSessionResultGroups: a picture entry -> {kind:'picture', entry}; a topic's FIRST non-blank text entry -> {kind:'text', topic, text} at that position (a later text of the same topic is dropped); the text of the Summary topic (isSummaryTopic) is NOT an item, it is `reply` (the first one), the agent's reply drawn LAST after every item; pictures filed under Summary stay in the stream. Mirrored x4.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "null blob",
        "raw": null,
        "expected": { "items": [], "reply": null }
      },
      {
        "name": "pictures and texts keep publish order, the summary becomes the reply",
        "raw": [
          { "topic": "Progress", "label": "Shot 1", "attachmentId": "a1", "inline": true, "caption": "Before" },
          { "topic": "nav", "label": null, "attachmentId": null, "text": "  The nav bar  " },
          { "topic": "nav", "label": "web", "attachmentId": "a2" },
          { "topic": "Summary", "label": null, "attachmentId": null, "text": " Shipped the nav. " },
          { "topic": "Progress", "label": "Shot 2", "attachmentId": "a3", "inline": true }
        ],
        "expected": {
          "items": [
            { "kind": "picture", "attachmentId": "a1" },
            { "kind": "text", "topic": "nav", "text": "The nav bar" },
            { "kind": "picture", "attachmentId": "a2" },
            { "kind": "picture", "attachmentId": "a3" }
          ],
          "reply": "Shipped the nav."
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "a topic's first text wins, blank texts and malformed rows drop, summary pictures stay",
        "raw": [
          { "topic": "nav", "label": null, "attachmentId": null, "text": "   " },
          { "topic": "nav", "label": null, "attachmentId": null, "text": "First" },
          { "topic": "nav", "label": null, "attachmentId": null, "text": "Second" },
          { "topic": "", "label": "x", "attachmentId": "a9" },
          "junk",
          { "topic": "summary", "label": "cover", "attachmentId": "a4" },
          { "topic": " SUMMARY ", "label": null, "attachmentId": null, "text": "One" },
          { "topic": "Summary", "label": null, "attachmentId": null, "text": "Two" }
        ],
        "expected": {
          "items": [
            { "kind": "text", "topic": "nav", "text": "First" },
            { "kind": "picture", "attachmentId": "a4" }
          ],
          "reply": "One"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "a JSON string blob reads like the array",
        "raw": "[{\"topic\":\"Progress\",\"label\":\"Shot 1\",\"attachmentId\":\"a1\",\"inline\":true}]",
        "expected": {
          "items": [{ "kind": "picture", "attachmentId": "a1" }],
          "reply": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "coverage": {
    "$comment": "EXP-1251: guideCoverage(groups, diffFiles). A group's listed path matches a diff file whose path equals it OR whose previousPath equals it; a section's files = the matched diff files in LISTED order (a file once), additions/deletions summed, fileCount = files; missing = listed paths no diff file matches. lead + sections come from guideSections (same numbering; the automatic section is never numbered). other = every diff file no group (lead included) matched, diff order, titled 'Other changes' (contract diffUi.guideOtherChanges) when there is at least one group, 'Changes' (diffUi.guideChangesRow) with none; null when nothing is left. complete = every diff file (the 'Show complete diff' row). diff null = not loaded: every changes null, missing [], other null, complete null. A file two sections name counts in both. Mirrored x4. guideFileCountLabel(n) = the row's muted count: '1 file' for one, else '<n> files' (fileCountLabels).",
    "fileCountLabels": [[0, "0 files"], [1, "1 file"], [6, "6 files"]],
    "cases": [
      {"name": "exact paths, a missing path and an unassigned file", "groups": [{"topic": "Summary", "files": ["a.ts"]}, {"topic": "nav", "files": ["b.ts", "gone.ts"]}], "diff": [{"path": "a.ts", "additions": 3, "deletions": 1}, {"path": "b.ts", "additions": 10, "deletions": 2}, {"path": "d.ts", "additions": 1, "deletions": 0}], "expected": {"lead": {"topic": "Summary", "files": ["a.ts"], "additions": 3, "deletions": 1, "missing": []}, "sections": [{"topic": "nav", "index": 1, "total": 1, "files": ["b.ts"], "additions": 10, "deletions": 2, "missing": ["gone.ts"]}], "other": {"topic": "Other changes", "files": ["d.ts"], "additions": 1, "deletions": 0}, "complete": {"fileCount": 3, "additions": 14, "deletions": 3}}},
      {"name": "a rename matches by its previous path, listed order wins", "groups": [{"topic": "move", "files": ["z.ts", "old/name.ts"]}], "diff": [{"path": "new/name.ts", "previousPath": "old/name.ts", "additions": 2, "deletions": 2}, {"path": "z.ts", "additions": 5, "deletions": 0}], "expected": {"lead": null, "sections": [{"topic": "move", "index": 1, "total": 1, "files": ["z.ts", "new/name.ts"], "additions": 7, "deletions": 2, "missing": []}], "other": null, "complete": {"fileCount": 2, "additions": 7, "deletions": 2}}},
      {"name": "a file two sections name counts in both", "groups": [{"topic": "one", "files": ["a.ts"]}, {"topic": "two", "files": ["a.ts", "b.ts"]}], "diff": [{"path": "a.ts", "additions": 1, "deletions": 1}, {"path": "b.ts", "additions": 4, "deletions": 0}], "expected": {"lead": null, "sections": [{"topic": "one", "index": 1, "total": 2, "files": ["a.ts"], "additions": 1, "deletions": 1, "missing": []}, {"topic": "two", "index": 2, "total": 2, "files": ["a.ts", "b.ts"], "additions": 5, "deletions": 1, "missing": []}], "other": null, "complete": {"fileCount": 2, "additions": 5, "deletions": 1}}},
      {"name": "no report: one Changes section holds the whole diff", "groups": [], "diff": [{"path": "a.ts", "additions": 1, "deletions": 0}, {"path": "b.ts", "additions": 0, "deletions": 6}], "expected": {"lead": null, "sections": [], "other": {"topic": "Changes", "files": ["a.ts", "b.ts"], "additions": 1, "deletions": 6}, "complete": {"fileCount": 2, "additions": 1, "deletions": 6}}},
      {"name": "a section without files claims nothing", "groups": [{"topic": "Verification", "files": []}], "diff": [{"path": "a.ts", "additions": 2, "deletions": 0}], "expected": {"lead": null, "sections": [{"topic": "Verification", "index": 1, "total": 1, "files": [], "additions": 0, "deletions": 0, "missing": []}], "other": {"topic": "Other changes", "files": ["a.ts"], "additions": 2, "deletions": 0}, "complete": {"fileCount": 1, "additions": 2, "deletions": 0}}},
      {"name": "an empty diff: every listed path is missing, nothing else", "groups": [{"topic": "nav", "files": ["a.ts"]}], "diff": [], "expected": {"lead": null, "sections": [{"topic": "nav", "index": 1, "total": 1, "files": [], "additions": 0, "deletions": 0, "missing": ["a.ts"]}], "other": null, "complete": {"fileCount": 0, "additions": 0, "deletions": 0}}},
      {"name": "no diff loaded", "groups": [{"topic": "Summary", "files": ["a.ts"]}, {"topic": "nav", "files": ["b.ts"]}], "diff": null, "expected": {"lead": {"topic": "Summary", "changes": null, "missing": []}, "sections": [{"topic": "nav", "index": 1, "total": 1, "changes": null, "missing": []}], "other": null, "complete": null}}
    ]
  },
  "prScope": {
    "$comment": "EXP-1251: a text entry may carry prUrl (the PR its topic belongs to, set when a run stacks a second PR). A topic's tag = its FIRST non-blank text entry's prUrl, trimmed (blank = untagged); its pictures follow it. sessionResultsForPr(raw, prUrl) keeps every entry of an untagged topic plus the topics tagged exactly prUrl, in order (prUrl null = untagged only); sessionResultPrUrls(raw) = every tag, first-seen. Mirrored x4.",
    "cases": [
      {"name": "a stacked second PR keeps its own topics", "raw": [{"topic": "Summary", "text": "iOS fix", "prUrl": "https://github.com/o/r/pull/1011"}, {"topic": "Verification", "text": "tests pass"}, {"topic": "Reviews", "text": "linked by pr_url", "prUrl": "https://github.com/o/r/pull/1012"}, {"topic": "Reviews", "label": "web", "attachmentId": "a1"}, {"topic": "Summary", "label": "ios", "attachmentId": "a2"}], "prUrls": ["https://github.com/o/r/pull/1011", "https://github.com/o/r/pull/1012"], "byPr": [{"prUrl": "https://github.com/o/r/pull/1011", "topics": ["Summary", "Verification", "Summary"]}, {"prUrl": "https://github.com/o/r/pull/1012", "topics": ["Verification", "Reviews", "Reviews"]}, {"prUrl": null, "topics": ["Verification"]}]},
      {"name": "an untagged report shows on every PR", "raw": [{"topic": "Summary", "text": "x", "prUrl": "  "}, {"topic": "nav", "label": "web", "attachmentId": "a1"}], "prUrls": [], "byPr": [{"prUrl": "https://github.com/o/r/pull/7", "topics": ["Summary", "nav"]}]}
    ]
  },
  "turns": {
    "$comment": "EXP-1245: sessionTurns(raw, feed) = the thread as TURNS for the run's owner. feed events: {kind:'user_message', at, text, images?} and {kind:'turn', state:'started'|'ended', at}, walked in at order (ties keep feed order). A user_message opens a new turn {message, startedAt: null}; when a turn was still running (started, not ended) it ends at the message's at and the new turn starts at that same at. A 'started' edge starts the newest turn if it has neither started nor ended, else opens a message-less turn unless one is running. An 'ended' edge ends the running turn (else ignored). Results entries carry the server's write stamp at (ms): each thread piece (sessionThread rules: a topic's first text, every picture, the Summary text = reply) lands in the LAST turn whose boundary (message at, else startedAt) <= at; a piece without at, or older than every boundary, lands in the first turn. No usable event (no feed) = ONE turn with today's thread and perTurn false. Mirrored x4.",
